{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/u684dv","slide":5,"text":"The key flow begins when staff click Call Next Patient. The browser sends the action to the application API. The server validates the staff account, completes the previous turn, and advances the next waiting entry. PostgreSQL saves the new state. Socket.IO then broadcasts a queue update. Every connected owner screen handles that event and updates the displayed current number, patient count, and status without a manual refresh."}
